      "value": "@{5a4aaf7f758fa46d131cd36b|full_name}: While I understand that a game needs to make money, it's weird to see Users actively asking for things that usually destroy a game. \n\nIf you research where VRC funding came from in the past, you may better understand why an ROI over ingame purchases thankfully wasn't their intention or something investors asked for. (Ask yourself how many overpriced trackers HTC would have sold without VRChat implementing them, being like the only game that supports them, then go check how much money HTC gave to VRC)\n\nIf VRC implements anything to make a profit, it is their business. But we do not need it as users and I dislike to see people actively screaming for a second life version of VRC. \n\nYou can buy models pre-configured for VRC already today (over paypal, on english sites from creators) and you may notice that this is usually not even wanted from VRC. Instead, most models are shared for free, and you can still support artists if you want to. This being said, the usual approach is that you can get avatars in the game from avatar worlds and all those prop features are already possible today. \n\nThis post doesn't ask for new features, it is only asking to make existing features a \"pay to play\" thing.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
