      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "In genaral a big NO - but a currency/shop system for creators to sell stuff they created like avatars/assets/shaders may be better than some external \"black market\". In general I want VRChat to stay as it is. Free. \n\nIngame currency could also allow people to take for example entrance fees to shows or lectures. Or we get some serverspace for free in the future and if we want to expand we have to rent more. Would make sense since that and traffic is one of the most expensive parts I guess.\n\nBut I dislike the way second life did it where you couldn't do anything without money. And micropayment for a \"pro\" SDK or a \"Premium\" Home is not the way I want it to go.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
